<WorksheetLayout
  title="Cause Finder"
  lesson="/courses/mfedu-2026/choose-your-cause/"
  intro="Every runway piece in this course tells a story that matters to its designer. This sheet helps you find yours."
>
  <h2>1. Brain dump</h2>
  <p>Set a timer for five minutes. List everything you care about — big or small, serious or silly. Don't judge, just write.</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>

  <h2>2. The "change one thing" test</h2>
  <p>If you could change one thing about each of these, what would it be?</p>
  <p><strong>My school:</strong></p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div></div>
  <p><strong>My neighborhood:</strong></p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div></div>
  <p><strong>The world:</strong></p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div></div>
  <p><strong>My own life:</strong></p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div></div>

  <h2>3. Pick two finalists</h2>
  <p>Circle the two ideas above you could imagine wearing on a runway. For each, answer:</p>
  <div class="ws-grid">
    <div>
      <p><strong>Cause A:</strong></p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div></div>
      <p class="ws-hint">Why does this matter to me?</p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>
      <p class="ws-hint">Who else cares about it?</p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p><strong>Cause B:</strong></p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div></div>
      <p class="ws-hint">Why does this matter to me?</p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>
      <p class="ws-hint">Who else cares about it?</p>
      <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>4. The pitch</h2>
  <p>Choose your cause and write the 30-second pitch you'll use to convince at least two classmates to join your design team.</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>

  <ul class="ws-checks">
    <li>I pitched my cause to the class</li>
    <li>At least two designers joined my team (or I joined theirs — that counts!)</li>
  </ul>
</WorksheetLayout>
